Changelog: 23-10-2026 07:16:27

Release 0.1.1.

Changelog: 23-10-2026 06:54:24

Fixed. The header's boxes are narrower: Controller says Edge or DualSense and Connection USB or Bluetooth (the full
names in their tooltips), so the widest value no longer widens them all. The update starts from an Update pill
(Firmware) in the same row instead of a small button beside the title (owner, 23-10-2026); it is orange when an update
can start, greyed (core's muted text for a pill that cannot be clicked) when it cannot, and its tooltip says
why.

Changelog: 23-10-2026 06:30:17

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 23-10-2026 06:11:43

Added. First version. USB HD Control shows Sony's DualSense (054c:0ce6) and DualSense Edge (054c:0df2) on Bazzite:
the header has the model, the connection (USB cable or Bluetooth), the battery (hid-playstation's power_supply, in
steps of 10 %), the firmware's update version and the latest one Sony offers; with more than one controller a list
chooses which. The kernel's hid-playstation keeps driving the controller; the app uses its hidraw node with the
standard library (HID feature report ioctls), every report padded to the size the report descriptor declares, as
Windows sends them. The firmware report (0x20) is read as hid-playstation reads it. The firmware update follows
dualsense-updater-rs (MIT, ported to Python): report 0xF4 sends the 256-byte header, the image in 32 KiB blocks of
57-byte pieces, verify and finalize, report 0xF5 is polled for each step's status (with a 60 s limit). Check for an
update reads Sony's info.json (fwupdater.dl.playstation.net), at window start at most once a day unless switched off;
Update firmware downloads the image from Sony's server, keeps it, refuses an image for another controller (its USB
product ID at 0x62 and target at 0x74) or one that is not newer (its update version at 0x78), saves a backup of the
Edge's profiles, and sends it over USB only. It does not start while another program (Steam) has the controller
open. Use a file sends an image of the user's own with the same checks. The images on Sony's server on 23-10-2026 are
known by their SHA-256 (DualSense Edge 0x0217, DualSense 0x0630 and 0x0641). The Edge's four profiles (reports 0x70
to 0x7B, layout from dualsense-edge-profile-web-application, MIT) are shown with their name, stick curves, trigger
ranges, remapped buttons and whether their CRC-32 matches; Back up saves the reports as JSON. The app does not write
profiles. --info prints the same without a window. Read on the owner's Edge (23-10-2026, on USB): update version
0x0200 built 21-06-2024 (Sony offers 0x0217), target 0044, its default profile with a matching CRC and three empty
slots, F4 64 bytes and F5 4 bytes in its descriptor. The owner updated that Edge with the window (23-10-2026,
06:27): from 0x0200 to Sony's 0x0217 (the known image), about 20 s from the profiles' backup to the controller leaving
USB, which came back 2 s later as firmware 0x0217 built 19-09-2025 (hid-playstation: fw_version 0x0100008b, hardware
unchanged); its profiles read back byte for byte as the backup made before the update. The confirmation says the
update takes about half a minute.
